  {
    "number": 63,
    "title": "Render shared agent monitoring as paged 64×64 dashboards",
    "body": "Refs #32.\n\nShared monitoring now produces a deterministic four-row 64×64 dashboard with attention-first stable ordering, ten-second pagination, explicit uncertainty and retained notices. Authenticated rendition reads return the exact RGB888 pixels and full layout details; synthetic browser examples use those same pixels. One active render and one latest pending snapshot bound work, and obsolete generations cannot publish.\n\nThis consumes #31's selected session source without provider interpretation, another state store, display takeover or physical commands. #33 retains the monitor panel and writer integration. Cadence defaults to an experimental 3000 ms and remains separate from physical qualification.\n\nValidation on `1a706478ce8f41ba2a1e1c0410c290894e614099`: Node 24 `npm ci`, `npm run check` passed 564 tests; `npm run test:browser` passed 56 desktop/mobile checks; post-sync workflow checks passed 16 current specifications, 17 archives and 10 fixtures. Focused missing-layout, missing-pixel-renderer, missing-service and missing-route failures were observed before implementation. Browser canvas bytes match RGB fixtures, and deterministic fake-device frames match those same bytes. Synthetic native/enlarged previews were visually inspected. The issue-linked OpenSpec change is synchronized and archived.\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews and current-head hosted CI are pending. Merge and merged-main CI remain required before tracking completion. The coordinator owns a Hub guide companion, currently being prepared; guide synchronization remains pending. Public publication, installation and physical acceptance are outside this source-only delivery.\n",
    "state": "open",
